---
/*
  Replaces /results. Structure and copy: 04-konzept.md section 4.3, page
  "/proof", and the record card definition in section 4.4.
  The metrics block from section 4.3, part 3, is deliberately not built yet:
  the income distribution of our own creators does not exist (concept 8.5,
  gap 1). An empty or estimated block is worse than none.
  Sprache: einfaches Englisch, Ansage Manuel 07.09.2026 abends.
*/
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import RecordCard from '../components/RecordCard.astro';
import CtaBlock from '../components/CtaBlock.astro';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';

const records = (await getCollection('records'))
  .filter((entry) => !entry.data.draft)
  .sort((a, b) => a.data.order - b.data.order);
---

<Base
  title="Proof | Wunder"
  description="How we report numbers: every number carries a time span, a starting point and a source, and every case says what did not work."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1>How we report numbers.</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Every number here carries three things. The time span it covers. The starting point we
        measured it against. And who read it, us or someone from outside. No number goes up
        without all three.
      </p>
      <p>
        That rule costs us the big round numbers other agencies put in their headline. We think
        you can tell the difference. That is the point.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Cases</h2>
      <p>
        One account each, with a date. Every case says what did not work. A case without that part
        is just an advert.
      </p>
      {
        records.length > 0 ? (
          <div class="cards">
            {records.map((entry) => (
              <RecordCard {...entry.data} />
            ))}
          </div>
        ) : (
          <div class="pending panel">
            <p>
              No case is ready yet. We are checking each one against the portal first. The stories
              from our old website are still up on the <a href="/results">results page</a>. Those
              are older, and they do not follow the rule above yet.
            </p>
          </div>
        )
      }
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>What is not on this page.</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>No screenshots of what someone earned.</li>
        <li>No press logos without the article behind them.</li>
        <li>No total without the group it was counted over.</li>
        <li>No quote with a name on it.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        The <a href="/results">results page</a> is the one exception. Those videos and stories come
        from our old website. Some creators show their face and their name there, because they
        agreed to it back then. They do not follow the rule on this page yet.
      </p>
      <p>
        We plan a page of numbers for all our creators. It goes up when the work behind it is
        done, and not one day before.
      </p>
      <CtaBlock secondary />
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .pending {
    margin-top: 32px;
    max-width: 640px;
  }

  .pending p {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .cards {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(320px, 1fr));
    gap: 24px;
    margin-top: 32px;
  }
</style>
